  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>(A)</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0023_649ca84dd7d0.png\" style=\"width: 218px; height: 150px;\" /></p><p>Morphine and many of its homologues, when administered in medicinal doses, relieve pain and produce sleep. In poisonous doses, these produce stupor, coma, convulsions and ultimately death. Morphine narcotics are sometimes referred to as opiates, since they are obtained from the opium poppy.</p><p>(B)</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0023_056d39cb2967.png\" style=\"width: 173px; height: 150px;\" /></p><p>Chloroxylenol used as an antiseptic</p><p>(C)</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0023_02e69c1c18cb.png\" style=\"width: 223px; height: 90px;\" /></p><p>Phenelzine (Nardil) use as Antidepressant</p><p>(D)</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0023_977f3d59e74b.png\" style=\"width: 149px; height: 150px;\" />​​​​​​​</p><p>Saccharin <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>550</mn></math> times sweeter than cane sugar</p></blockquote>"
